# --- Build-context exclusions for packages/super-sync-server/Dockerfile ---
# Both call sites build with the REPO ROOT as context (`context: .` in
# .github/workflows/supersync-docker.yml, "$REPO_ROOT" in scripts/build-and-push.sh), so
# this file is the only .dockerignore Docker reads — a package-level one would be ignored.
# The bare patterns above match at the root only, never at packages/super-sync-server/**.
#
# .gitignore has no bearing on a build context, so without these the builder stage sweeps
# in whatever is on the maintainer's disk. The multi-stage build keeps it out of the
# published layer today, but that is one COPY edit away from being untrue.

# Secrets and live configuration, anywhere in the tree. `**/.env` does not match
# `.env.local` / `.env.production`, hence the separate glob.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/secrets/
**/tde-keys/

# Never let a local install shadow the image's own `npm ci` result, and keep test
# artifacts out of the build context entirely.
**/node_modules
**/coverage
**/*.log

# Local server state
packages/super-sync-server/data/
packages/super-sync-server/backups/
packages/super-sync-server/initdb.d/
packages/super-sync-server/.health-alert/

# Rendered at runtime from the shipped templates. A stale copy would bake one operator's
# legal identity into the image every other operator pulls.
packages/super-sync-server/public/privacy.html
packages/super-sync-server/public/index.html
packages/super-sync-server/public/terms.html

# Our hosted instance's Terms of Service — names German law, a Leipzig venue and our own
# contact address. Operators supply their own via <DATA_DIR>/legal/terms.html.
packages/super-sync-server/legal/
